meta {
  name: 08 Assign Operator Permissions
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/manage/{{operatorUserId}}/branch-permissions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAdminToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "branchId": "{{branchId}}",
    "items": [
      { "moduleKey": "accession", "permissionKey": "accession:in_house_order__collect_the_sample", "allowed": true },
      { "moduleKey": "accession", "permissionKey": "accession:in_house_order__accept_the_sample", "allowed": true }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  **Step 4b — Grant the operator the two accession permissions the flow needs.**

  The accession **Collect** and **Accept** transitions are RBAC-enforced
  (`@RequirePermission(ACC_IH_COLLECT / ACC_IH_ACCEPT)`), so the branch-scoped
  operator must hold them:
  - `accession:in_house_order__collect_the_sample`
  - `accession:in_house_order__accept_the_sample`

  `permissionKey` = `moduleKey:section__action` (from the permission catalog —
  `GET /users/manage/permission-catalog`); only modules enabled at the **branch**
  are accepted, so this works because step 04 enabled `accession` on the branch
  (the grant is independent of the operator's own module set — the `receptionist`
  role template doesn't include `accession`, but the direct permission grant is
  what the guard checks). Order creation (`registration`) and report reads are not
  blocked for the operator, and lab-test creation is done by the Business Admin
  (bypass) in step 14 — so no other grants are needed here.
}
